# Shell scripts reach the working tree with LF line endings on every platform.
#
# `.github/scripts/assert-toolchain.sh` is run by the Windows job, and on
# Windows the default `core.autocrlf=true` would check it out with CRLF. That
# turns out to be survivable — Git Bash 2.47.1 runs the CRLF copy of this
# script and produces the correct answer, because MSYS2's bash strips the
# carriage returns — but that is a patch in one bash rather than a property of
# bash, and the job it would break is the one that cannot be tried locally.
# Two lines here is a cheaper way to be sure than finding out on a push.
*.sh text eol=lf
